{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463280",
      "title": "Rendering Lists of Data",
      "lectureOrder": 46,
      "videoOrder": 41,
      "sourceHash": "807e88205d8f67b95498119a76137308a7ef6745a80026cb208583e361c6d83c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 4.21,
          "en": "So we learned about v-if,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.21,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "which is great for showing content conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 10.93,
          "en": "but we all have an array of content here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.93,
          "end": 12.97,
          "en": "potentially we have multiple goals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.97,
          "end": 16.93,
          "en": "and it would be nice if we could output those actual goals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.93,
          "end": 18.97,
          "en": "which we store in our view app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.97,
          "end": 22.163,
          "en": "instead of this dummy goal goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.09,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "Well, of course view has us covered for that, as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 30.1,
          "en": "We now need to output a list of content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.1,
          "end": 33.65,
          "en": "and that's also something you commonly have to do in apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.65,
          "end": 36.96,
          "en": "consider lists of products, users' to do's,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.96,
          "end": 40.02,
          "en": "lists are everywhere in web apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.02,
          "end": 42.82,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, view gives us a tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.82,
          "end": 44.72,
          "en": "for working with lists of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.72,
          "end": 47.24,
          "en": "and outputting repeated content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.24,
          "end": 50.52,
          "en": "Here we wanna repeat this list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.52,
          "end": 54.49,
          "en": "with different content for all the goals we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.49,
          "end": 56.98,
          "en": "And view has another directive for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.98,
          "end": 58.633,
          "en": "The v-for directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.74,
          "end": 61.68,
          "en": "And you might see a pattern here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 66.68,
          "en": "We have v-if, just as we have if statements in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.7,
          "end": 72.7,
          "en": "And we have v-for just as we have for loops in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.58,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "for dealing with repeated code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 78.223,
          "en": "And it's the same logic here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.223,
          "end": 82.873,
          "en": "V-for is there to help us output content that's repeated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.37,
          "end": 87.39,
          "en": "So for example here, we wanna output the same list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "over and over again for every goal which we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 93.87,
          "en": "And we can do this by setting up value to v-for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.87,
          "end": 95.65,
          "en": "and between those double quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.65,
          "end": 98,
          "en": "as always, with those view features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98,
          "end": 101.21000000000001,
          "en": "we can execute a JavaScript expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.21000000000001,
          "end": 104.66,
          "en": "And here we can point at goals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.66,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "which is our data property that holds the goal's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 110.03,
          "en": "But not just like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.03,
          "end": 112.28,
          "en": "instead in a for loop in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.28,
          "end": 115.68,
          "en": "we have something like const goal of goals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 119.4,
          "en": "This is how a for loop could look like in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.4,
          "end": 121.64,
          "en": "It looks quite similar in view.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.64,
          "end": 124.37,
          "en": "Here, we wanna go through all goals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.37,
          "end": 127.48,
          "en": "but of course we also wanna get hold of each goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.48,
          "end": 130.84,
          "en": "so that we can take that goal's text for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.84,
          "end": 133.95,
          "en": "and output it between the list item text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.95,
          "end": 137.36,
          "en": "That's why the v-for syntax looks a bit different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.36,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "we have goal in goals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 143.39,
          "en": "Goal of goals also is supported but you should use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.39,
          "end": 145.02,
          "en": "goal in goals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.02,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "Which is a bit different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 148.56,
          "en": "than the standard for loop in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.56,
          "end": 151.3,
          "en": "but you just have to memorize it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.3,
          "end": 154.81,
          "en": "v loop, through an array, with the in keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.81,
          "end": 158.11,
          "en": "when using v-for and now this name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.11,
          "end": 159.4,
          "en": "goal in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.4,
          "end": 160.45,
          "en": "is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.45,
          "end": 164.69,
          "en": "You can name it G or GO or hello, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.69,
          "end": 166.31,
          "en": "I'm going to go for goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.31,
          "end": 170.15,
          "en": "because this will hold every goal in goals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.15,
          "end": 174.48,
          "en": "for every iteration v-for does for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.48,
          "end": 177.52,
          "en": "And v-for will go through all the goals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.52,
          "end": 180.43,
          "en": "and give us access to every goal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.43,
          "end": 182.13,
          "en": "And why is that useful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.13,
          "end": 185.66,
          "en": "Well, our goals are just strings, in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.66,
          "end": 187.84,
          "en": "We just add whatever the user entered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.84,
          "end": 190.04,
          "en": "which is a string, to goals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.04,
          "end": 192.99,
          "en": "So goals is an array full of strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.99,
          "end": 196.37,
          "en": "So every goal here is also just a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.37,
          "end": 197.29,
          "en": "enhanced here between",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.29,
          "end": 199.69,
          "en": "the opening of the closing list item tack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.69,
          "end": 202.06,
          "en": "we can use double curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.06,
          "end": 203.983,
          "en": "to output goal like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.32,
          "end": 207.18,
          "en": "And this now has to be goal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.18,
          "end": 208.65,
          "en": "if you used goal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 208.65,
          "end": 211.6,
          "en": "If you used hello here, for whatever reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 211.6,
          "end": 214.73,
          "en": "it has to be hello here, as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.73,
          "end": 217.423,
          "en": "But I'm using goal so let's revert to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 218.32,
          "end": 220.55,
          "en": "Now what this does, is, it tells view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 220.55,
          "end": 222.62,
          "en": "that it should repeat this list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 223.54,
          "end": 226.15,
          "en": "for all the goals in goals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.15,
          "end": 229.6,
          "en": "so render as many list items as we have goals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.6,
          "end": 231.15,
          "en": "in the goals array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.15,
          "end": 233,
          "en": "and give us access to every goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 233,
          "end": 235.89,
          "en": "and then inside, and that's really important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 235.89,
          "end": 238.59,
          "en": "inside of the v-for controlled element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.59,
          "end": 242.33,
          "en": "so between the opening and closing tags of that element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.33,
          "end": 244.54,
          "en": "and also on the element itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 244.54,
          "end": 246.53,
          "en": "we have access to that goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.53,
          "end": 248.3,
          "en": "We don't have access to goal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 248.3,
          "end": 251.65,
          "en": "outside of the list item element here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 251.65,
          "end": 255.86,
          "en": "So if I tried to output goal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 255.86,
          "end": 257.52,
          "en": "in another paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 257.52,
          "end": 260,
          "en": "which is not inside of the list item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 260,
          "end": 261.99,
          "en": "that would not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 261.99,
          "end": 264.01,
          "en": "And I guess that makes a lot of sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 264.01,
          "end": 265.62,
          "en": "In regular JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 265.62,
          "end": 267.4,
          "en": "if you have a for loop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 267.4,
          "end": 269.15,
          "en": "even though it looks a bit different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 269.15,
          "end": 273.48,
          "en": "if you have for loop here, you also can't use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 273.48,
          "end": 275.99,
          "en": "constant outside of the for loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 275.99,
          "end": 277.707,
          "en": "And it's the same with v-for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 278.94,
          "end": 281.38,
          "en": "So now just we'll repeat as many list items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 281.38,
          "end": 283.26,
          "en": "as we need for all our goals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 283.26,
          "end": 286.28,
          "en": "and output the goal text in our case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 286.28,
          "end": 288.2,
          "en": "between the list item tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 288.2,
          "end": 291.84000000000003,
          "en": "So for now I've saved it, and reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 291.84000000000003,
          "end": 293.48,
          "en": "we can add finish the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 293.48,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "click add goal, and here is our goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 298.43,
          "en": "We can also add master view,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 298.43,
          "end": 301.08,
          "en": "click add goal, and here's the second goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 301.08,
          "end": 305.46,
          "en": "And you see that this list grows with every new item we add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 305.46,
          "end": 307.85,
          "en": "And this is v for and why it matters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 307.85,
          "end": 311.78,
          "en": "because now we can really build a dynamic application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 311.78,
          "end": 316.32,
          "en": "where we render lists of content and also update that list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 316.32,
          "end": 318.26,
          "en": "when the content changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 318.26,
          "end": 320.76,
          "en": "And view does that updating for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 320.76,
          "end": 323.253,
          "en": "and it also does it in a smart way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 324.09,
          "end": 328.12,
          "en": "If you inspect the list item here with the depth tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 328.12,
          "end": 330.21,
          "en": "I mentioned before that the parts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 330.21,
          "end": 334.05,
          "en": "which are updated in the DOM, will flash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 334.05,
          "end": 335.8,
          "en": "So if I add a new goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 335.8,
          "end": 338.84000000000003,
          "en": "watch what happens here on the right to those first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 338.84000000000003,
          "end": 341.22,
          "en": "two existing list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 341.22,
          "end": 342.053,
          "en": "You see?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 342.053,
          "end": 343.53,
          "en": "They did not flash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 343.53,
          "end": 346.2,
          "en": "Only the third one, the new one did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 346.2,
          "end": 348.73,
          "en": "And that is how view updates the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 348.73,
          "end": 351.11,
          "en": "it does it in a very efficient way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 351.11,
          "end": 353.74,
          "en": "leaving the unchanged list items alone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 353.74,
          "end": 355.79,
          "en": "and only adding a new list item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 355.79,
          "end": 357.97,
          "en": "which, of course, is great for performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 357.97,
          "end": 361.87,
          "en": "It would be bad if view would re-render the entire list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 361.87,
          "end": 363.66,
          "en": "with every new item that we add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 363.66,
          "end": 365.7,
          "en": "This would not be good for performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 365.7,
          "end": 368.43,
          "en": "and thankfully view doesn't do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 368.43,
          "end": 371.16,
          "en": "It's just important to be aware of such things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 371.16,
          "end": 373.51,
          "en": "because that helps you understand a bit more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
